From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: shader model 5 (stage 1) and texture/control flow fixes for virgl

Towards feature level 11_0 natively (TGSI through virgl). Stage 1: shader model 5 parsing and the instructions of
vertex, geometry and pixel shaders. Found on the way, D3D10 bugs on virgl that this fixes too:

- Control flow: virglrenderer has no TGSI CONT, SWITCH/CASE/DEFAULT/ENDSWITCH (it drops them), so HLSL continue and
  switch ran wrong. Lowered: a loop with a continue runs its body in an inner loop that runs once, a switch is a
  loop that runs once around if-regions per case label group (fall-through kept); flags carry break/continue out.
- Textures: the virgl path sampled through the sampler register's slot (t3 with s0 read texture 0), ignored the
  texture operand's swizzle (fxc writes single channels with it), texel offsets, the comparison of sample_c (no
  shadow target), resinfo's return type and declared no sampler view types (integer textures). Now each (t#, s#,
  comparison) combination gets a TGSI sampler of its own with the view's target and return type, bound at draw
  time (Shader_tex_slots, ShaderBindTexSlots); results are swizzled; offsets, shadow targets (reference in .z/.w or
  a second operand, level 0 through zero gradients), resinfo/bufinfo conversions, ld2dms' sample index.
- New: gather4 (component select, _c, _po with register offsets), lod, sampleinfo, samplepos (standard patterns),
  rcp, coarse/fine derivatives, countbits, firstbit_lo/hi/shi, bfrev, ubfe/ibfe/bfi (D3D's results past bit 31),
  f32tof16 (round toward zero, like WARP)/f16tof32 by integer arithmetic (no half packing in virgl), uaddc, usubb,
  swapc, emit/cut on streams, GS instance count/ID, SV_Coverage in/out, SV_SampleIndex, conservative depth outputs,
  centroid/sample interpolation, eval_centroid/sample_index/snapped. The parser knows every shader model 5 opcode
  (236, unknown ones are skipped instead of misparsed), 3D operand indices and the new declarations.
- The translator's state (4096 temporaries) lives on the heap: on the stack it overflowed DWM's thread (crash loop,
  black desktop) once the translator grew.
- BC6H/BC7 formats (BPTC).
- Development: WINBOAT_D3D_FL11=1 in a program's environment reports feature level 11_0 (with the compute cap the
  runtime requires) to that program only, for testing while compute and tessellation are missing.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Adapter.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Adapter.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Adapter.cpp
@@ -211,11 +211,27 @@
    }
    memset(pData->pData, 0, pData->DataSize);
    switch (pData->Type) {
+   case D3D11DDICAPS_SHADER: {
+      /* The runtime refuses feature level 11_0 without compute (and raw/structured buffers) in shader model 4.x
+       * too. XXX development: compute shaders are stage 2 of feature level 11_0; only with the switch below. */
+      char fl11[4] = "";
+      if (pData->DataSize >= sizeof(D3D11DDI_SHADER_CAPS) &&
+          GetEnvironmentVariableA("WINBOAT_D3D_FL11", fl11, sizeof fl11) && fl11[0] == '1') {
+         static_cast<D3D11DDI_SHADER_CAPS *>(pData->pData)->Caps =
+            D3D11DDICAPS_SHADER_COMPUTE_PLUS_RAW_AND_STRUCTURED_BUFFERS_IN_SHADER_4_X;
+      }
+      break;
+   }
    case D3D11DDICAPS_3DPIPELINESUPPORT:
-      /* The 11.x DDI runtime asks which feature levels the device has: 10_0 */
+      /* The 11.x DDI runtime asks which feature levels the device has: 10_0. Development: 11_0 for programs
+       * started with WINBOAT_D3D_FL11=1, while shader model 5 is being completed (test programs only). */
       if (pData->DataSize >= sizeof(D3D11DDI_3DPIPELINESUPPORT_CAPS)) {
+         char fl11[4] = "";
+         bool dev_fl11 = GetEnvironmentVariableA("WINBOAT_D3D_FL11", fl11, sizeof fl11) && fl11[0] == '1';
          static_cast<D3D11DDI_3DPIPELINESUPPORT_CAPS *>(pData->pData)->Caps =
-            D3D11DDI_ENCODE_3DPIPELINESUPPORT_CAP(D3D11DDI_3DPIPELINELEVEL_10_0);
+            D3D11DDI_ENCODE_3DPIPELINESUPPORT_CAP(D3D11DDI_3DPIPELINELEVEL_10_0) |
+            (dev_fl11 ? D3D11DDI_ENCODE_3DPIPELINESUPPORT_CAP(D3D11DDI_3DPIPELINELEVEL_10_1) |
+                        D3D11DDI_ENCODE_3DPIPELINESUPPORT_CAP(D3D11DDI_3DPIPELINELEVEL_11_0) : 0);
       }
       break;
    default:
